[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: The legend is the narrative with the legend widget anywhere in a root's tree, drawn once where its PLACE puts it

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[DECISION]
UID: DEC-LEGEND-IS-DATA-WHERE-PLACED
TITLE: The legend is the narrative with the legend widget anywhere in a root's tree, drawn once where its PLACE puts it
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATUS: accepted
RETIRES_ON: Two roots need to share one legend and repeating it proves to drift.
STATEMENT: >>>
What DEC-LEGEND-IS-DATA said stands: the words a view's rows may carry, their
colours and their meanings are rows of one narrative whose WIDGET is legend
('- WORD: colour: meaning'), never a grammar field and never renderer
knowledge. What is replaced is where it sits: not 'a child of the root' by
definition, but wherever its PLACE puts it -- a card on Start, drawn once and
nowhere else. A legend row may carry a fourth part, the label the row's
by-line takes ('- FALLS OUT: slate: dissolved; the direction replaces it:
Dissolved by'), so the renderer never knows which word means 'owned' and
which 'dissolved'.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The 'child of the root' clause composed with the old tab rule into a legend that was both a card on Start and a tab of its own. The vocabulary itself was right.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Ruled 2026-08-30 as a first-pass decision under the operator's delegation ('I don't want to be bothered by the recommendation before implementation'); overrule by superseding. Chosen from three independent designs judged against an 82-element inventory of the v1 page. AUTHORED_BY reads llm because the writer has no flag for the human rungs.
<<<
